{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>נער</b> — I tested this in my youth and have grown old." "<b>נעזב</b> — utterly, as in: כי לא אעזבך (for I will not abandon you), and he sought bread and a garment." "<b>וזרעו</b> — the little one whom he left, on account of the merit of the father, all the days of his life — shall live in good, and his seed after him for a blessing, as in כל רואיו ברכוהו."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:01.169220540Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}